{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>They shall burn him and them.</b> You cannot say his first wife — for he married her permitted and she was not forbidden to him. Rather, Scripture writes here 'a woman and her mother' — both of them forbidden: that he married his mother-in-law and her mother. And some of our teachers say: there is only his mother-in-law here; and what is 'them'? One of them — and it is a Greek locution, הֵן = one. (Sifra; Sanhedrin 76a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:24.698816781Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}